          "type": "output_text",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "{\"occurrence_id\":\"dumas-fils-la-dame-aux-camelias-dbb35581cef3\",\"core_classification\":{\"label_support\":{\"truth_conditional\":4,\"performative\":0,\"exclamatory_reflexive\":0,\"other\":0},\"confidence\":0.94,\"analysis\":\"“Je vous aime” is principally a written avowal presenting the writer’s love as true. It also reassures the addressee after she cancels that evening’s meeting, but the core words do not independently undertake a commitment, and there is no evidence that they are a reflex-like expressive discharge.\",\"ambiguity\":\"The message may have a strategic or compensatory purpose, but the excerpt does not establish insincerity; in any case, sincerity is orthogonal to its truth-conditional mode.\"},\"other_diagnosis\":{\"tpe_failure\":null,\"core_not_context\":null},\"utterance_status\":{\"status\":\"written\",\"description\":\"A written message or note is quoted within the narration; the classified event is the writer’s closing sentence, “Je vous aime.”\"},\"contextual_interpretation\":\"The avowal closes an affectionate message explaining that illness and medical orders prevent a meeting that evening, while promising a meeting the next day. Its placement after “pour vous récompenser” gives it a reassuring, possibly compensatory interpersonal role, but that contextual function does not turn the core sentence into a commitment or an expressive reflex.\",\"evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"e1\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“Je vous aime.”\",\"supports\":\"The unqualified declarative directly presents the writer’s loving state as true, strongly supporting T.\",\"confidence\":0.99},{\"evidence_id\":\"e2\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“Cher enfant, je suis un peu souffrante, et le médecin m'ordonne le repos.”\",\"supports\":\"The affectionate address and explanatory prose frame the avowal as part of a composed personal message rather than a reflex-like verbal discharge.\",\"confidence\":0.94},{\"evidence_id\":\"e3\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“Mais, pour vous récompenser, je vous attendrai demain à midi. Je vous aime.”\",\"supports\":\"The avowal follows cancellation and rescheduling, giving it a reassuring or compensatory contextual role; the explicit future undertaking belongs to the preceding sentence rather than to the core love utterance.\",\"confidence\":0.96}],\"background_knowledge\":{\"used\":false,\"familiarity\":\"none\",\"confidence\":null,\"contribution\":null},\"ontology_assessment\":{\"fit\":\"natural\",\"diagnosis\":\"T naturally captures the core written avowal. Its reassuring placement and composed delivery are contextual features adequately described without adding P, E, or O.\",\"candidate_recurrent_dimension\":null},\"notes\":null}"
        }
